    99	      <section id="the-catch" data-layer="fact">
   100	        <aside class="the-catch" data-layer="fact">
   101	          <p class="tt-label">The catch</p>
   102	          <p>The public accounts identify pressure and participants, but they do not establish one published chain of contractual authority. They also collapse four different tour roles when they describe every departure as an opening act.</p>
   103	          <ol>
   104	            <li>
   105	              <h3>Who held final authority remains unresolved.</h3>
   106	              <p>Macklemore attributed the removal to Sheeran and his team. Sheeran attributed it to the promoter and said the venues and promoter made the final decision. Messina said venues would not accept the lineup. The industry participants interviewed by AP were not involved in this tour, and no executed contract is in the admitted record.<Cite s="macklemore-removal-statement-2026-09-14" passage="Ed Sheeran and his team have made the decision to remove me from The Loop tour." /><Cite s="ed-sheeran-response-2026-09-15" passage="Macklemore coming off tour was the promoter's decision, it was not mine." /><Cite s="rolling-stone-removal-2026-09-14" passage="we have been notified by venues on the upcoming U.S. tour dates" /><Cite s="ap-tour-power-2026-09-17" passage="Neither Gary nor Waddell nor Serwin are involved in the Sheeran tour." /></p>
   107	            </li>
   108	            <li>
   109	              <h3>Four artists left, but they were not four remaining openers.</h3>
   110	              <p>Rowe and Lukas Graham were replacement U.S. support acts. Beoga described itself as Sheeran's band for the remaining U.S. tour. Finneas was scheduled for South America later in the year.<Cite s="ap-support-acts-2026-09-15" passage="Rowe and Lukas Graham would have been replacements for Macklemore on Sheeran’s remaining U.S. dates" /><Cite s="beoga-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="depart as Ed Sheeran's band on the remaining US Loop tour" /><Cite s="ap-support-acts-2026-09-15" passage="Finneas, who is Billie Eilish’s brother and musical collaborator, was due to tour with Sheeran in South America later this year" /></p>
   111	            </li>
   112	          </ol>
   113	        </aside>
   114	      </section>
   115	
   116	      <section id="why-others-left" data-layer="fact">
   117	        <SectionKicker text="Four decisions, four roles" />
   118	        <h2 data-layer="fact">Why the other artists left</h2>
   119	
   120	        <p data-layer="narrative">Finneas said artists should not be silenced when they speak for oppressed people and withdrew from his upcoming dates with Sheeran.<Cite s="finneas-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="Artists must not be silenced when they speak up for the oppressed. I have decided to withdraw from my upcoming tour dates with Ed Sheeran." /></p>
   121	
   122	        <p data-layer="narrative">Aaron Rowe withdrew as a North American support act. He said he could not accept billionaires using their power to silence people who speak up.<Cite s="aaron-rowe-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="I have made the decision to withdraw as a support act for Ed Sheeran's The Loop North American Tour." /><Cite s="aaron-rowe-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="I cannot stand by and allow billionaires to use their position of power to silence the rightful voices of those who speak up" /></p>
   123	
   124	        <p data-layer="narrative">Beoga departed as Sheeran's band for the remaining U.S. dates. The band said it would not play venues that silence artists for saying “Free Palestine.”<Cite s="beoga-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="We have made the decision to depart as Ed Sheeran's band on the remaining US Loop tour" /><Cite s="beoga-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="we will not play in venues that silence artists for saying Free Palestine" /></p>
   125	
   126	        <p data-layer="narrative">Lukas Graham objected to wealth determining who gets to speak and withdrew from the remaining dates. The band's statement also cautioned that there was not one single reason for its decision.<Cite s="lukas-graham-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="Nobody's bank balance should decide who gets to speak or which suffering we're allowed to acknowledge." /><Cite s="lukas-graham-withdrawal-2026-09-15" passage="We're withdrawing from the remaining dates. There isn't one single reason behind this decision." /></p>
   127	
   128	        <DataTable columns={["Artist", "Scheduled role", "Recorded action"]} rows={lineupRows} caption="The roles named in the September 15 records" />
   129	
   130	        <SourcedBlock source="rolling-stone-aaron-rowe-followup-2026-09-18" kind="record" detail>
   131	          <p>Rowe later said the criticism should focus on Kraft rather than Sheeran, while maintaining that Macklemore should not have been removed.<Cite s="rolling-stone-aaron-rowe-followup-2026-09-18" passage="when you really should be focusing on the likes of [New England Patriots owner] Robert Kraft." /><Cite s="rolling-stone-aaron-rowe-followup-2026-09-18" passage="Rowe affirmed that he didn’t think Macklemore should’ve been pulled off the tour" /></p>
   132	        </SourcedBlock>
   133	      </section>
   134	
   135	      <section id="what-happened-next" data-layer="fact">
   136	        <SectionKicker text="Philadelphia" />
   137	        <h2 data-layer="fact">What happened next</h2>
   138	
   139	        <p data-layer="narrative">On September 17, CAIR-Philadelphia filed a Pennsylvania Right-to-Know request for communications, decision records, policies, contracts and other records concerning Macklemore's removal from the Philadelphia lineup.<Cite s="cair-philadelphia-records-request-2026-09-17" passage="submitted a Pennsylvania Right-to-Know Law request seeking records concerning the decision that resulted in rapper Macklemore being removed from the lineup" /><Cite s="cair-philadelphia-records-request-2026-09-17" passage="Any policy, contractual provision, safety consideration, agreement, or other standard cited as authority for excluding or restricting a performer" /></p>
   140	
   141	        <p data-layer="narrative">The Philadelphia concert went ahead on September 19. Sheeran began alone, without an opener, and other musicians joined him later in the show.<Cite s="ap-philadelphia-outcome-2026-09-19" passage="Sheeran began the concert alone on stage with no opener, but was joined by other musicians later in the show." /></p>
   142	
   143	        <p data-layer="narrative">Sheeran called the situation in Gaza “catastrophic and unjustifiable” and said he worried about venues preapproving performances. A small group of pro-Palestinian demonstrators gathered outside the stadium before the show.<Cite s="ap-philadelphia-outcome-2026-09-19" passage="what is happening in Gaza “catastrophic and unjustifiable.”" /><Cite s="ap-philadelphia-outcome-2026-09-19" passage="He also told fans he worries about venues preapproving performances." /><Cite s="ap-philadelphia-outcome-2026-09-19" passage="Before Saturday’s show, a small group of pro-Palestinian demonstrators congregated outside the stadium." /></p>
   144	
   145	        <p data-layer="narrative">The records request expressly says it does not presume what responsive records will show. As of September 20, no response or production is in the admitted record.<Cite s="cair-philadelphia-records-request-2026-09-17" passage="the request does not presume what those records will show" /></p>
   146	
