checks/reader-models/ed-sheeran-tour--2026-09-14-macklemore-removed-from-the-loop-tour.md:5:A stranger arrives having seen that Macklemore was removed from Ed Sheeran's tour and that the remaining opening acts quit, with four departures and 10 remaining North American shows as the numbers most likely to stick. They may read that as Sheeran personally firing Macklemore and every opener then abandoning the tour, although the four artists held different roles and the public record does not settle final contractual authority (`ap-support-acts-2026-09-15`, `ed-sheeran-response-2026-09-15`, `ap-tour-power-2026-09-17`). Before the removal, Macklemore had played two MetLife dates and was scheduled for eight of the 10 shows left (`ed-sheeran-past-tour-dates-2026-09-20`, `rolling-stone-removal-2026-09-14`).
checks/reader-models/ed-sheeran-tour--2026-09-14-macklemore-removed-from-the-loop-tour.md:9:1. What happened: On September 14, Macklemore was removed from eight scheduled remaining Loop Tour appearances after venues objected, and on September 15 Finneas, Aaron Rowe, Lukas Graham and Beoga withdrew from different supporting roles (`rolling-stone-removal-2026-09-14`, `ap-support-acts-2026-09-15`).
checks/reader-models/ed-sheeran-tour--2026-09-14-macklemore-removed-from-the-loop-tour.md:10:2. Why it matters to someone who does not follow this subject: The dispute shows how venue, promoter and headliner power can determine who appears and what reaches a stadium audience, while one lineup decision prompted four artists to leave in opposition to perceived silencing (`ap-tour-power-2026-09-17`, `finneas-withdrawal-2026-09-15`, `aaron-rowe-withdrawal-2026-09-15`, `lukas-graham-withdrawal-2026-09-15`, `beoga-withdrawal-2026-09-15`).
checks/reader-models/ed-sheeran-tour--2026-09-14-macklemore-removed-from-the-loop-tour.md:11:3. The easiest wrong reading, the one the headline or the coverage invites: Sheeran did not simply fire Macklemore and lose all remaining opening acts; Gillette's refusal is confirmed, broader venue pressure is supported, final contractual authority is unresolved, and the four departures covered replacement openers, Sheeran's band and a later South American support slot (`usa-today-kraft-2026-09-14`, `ed-sheeran-response-2026-09-15`, `rolling-stone-removal-2026-09-14`, `ap-support-acts-2026-09-15`).
checks/reader-models/ed-sheeran-tour--2026-09-14-macklemore-removed-from-the-loop-tour.md:12:4. The one concept a stranger must hold to follow it, the mechanism: A promoter finances and contracts a tour, a venue can refuse to host a lineup, and a stadium-level headliner ordinarily has substantial approval, but the general model does not reveal this tour's unpublished contract rights (`ap-tour-power-2026-09-17`, `ed-sheeran-response-2026-09-15`).
checks/reader-models/ed-sheeran-tour--2026-09-14-macklemore-removed-from-the-loop-tour.md:14:6. What is unresolved as of the newest dated record: The public record does not establish final contractual authority, every objecting venue and communication, whether Kraft coordinated the broader pressure, or the rebuilt lineup for the remaining dates (`ed-sheeran-response-2026-09-15`, `rolling-stone-removal-2026-09-14`, `ap-tour-power-2026-09-17`, `gap-cair-philadelphia-records-request`).
